About the Role

You’ll support our Legal Team across LATAM and other international jurisdictions, focusing on betting and gaming regulations, contracts and general legal matters. Your responsibilities will include reviewing and drafting contracts and legal documents, conducting legal research, supporting litigation matters, handling corporate housekeeping and maintaining the legal library, all under the supervision of the Legal Counsel. The role will also provide exposure to broader international legal matters, including commercial contracts, corporate governance and regulatory topics, as well as opportunities to assist with regulatory and certification processes, such as audits, submissions and communications with testing laboratories and regulators, depending on business needs.

What you'll do:

• Review, draft and negotiate commercial agreements (vendor, service, marketing, sponsorship, affiliate, NDAs, data processing), flagging risks and proposing mitigations to the Legal Counsel

• Review corporate, regulatory and commercial documents (policies, terms and conditions, powers of attorney, board resolutions, filings) for accuracy and consistency

• Keep the legal library and contract repository up to date, with version control, templates, standard clauses, a central register of contracts and key dates (renewals, expiries, notice periods), and an internal knowledge base

• Support litigation and administrative proceedings by gathering documents and evidence, tracking deadlines, coordinating with external counsel, and preparing case summaries and status reports

• Carry out legal and regulatory research (contracts, consumer, data protection, corporate, betting/gaming law) and draft junior-level memos and opinions

• Help with corporate housekeeping: entity records, corporate acts, registrations and filings

• Support regulatory and certification processes when needed: tracking certificate and report expiry dates, preparing documents for audits and regulator submissions, and liaising with testing labs;

• Assist the Compliance teams (Brazil, Mexico and other markets.) with policy drafts, regulatory checks and internal processes;

• Handle internal legal requests from business teams (Product, Marketing, Finance, HR), sorting and routing them under the Legal Counsel’s supervision;

• Prepare reports and status updates for leadership and stakeholders;

• Support certification and compliance projects end-to-end: scheduling, tracking progress, coordinating with testing labs (ATFs), preparing documentation for audits and regulator submissions;

• Interface with external certification bodies, testing labs, third-party vendors, and regulators;

• Prepare reports, dashboards and status updates for leadership &amp; stakeholders

What you'll bring:

• Complete Law bachelor's degree and active BAR membership;

• Fluent English and Spanish (written &amp; spoken) are mandatory.&nbsp;

• Attention to detail, strong organizational skills, ability to manage multiple certification tracks

• Analytical mindset, capacity to learn technical standards (software, testing, gaming)

• Proactive, good communicator, ability to liaise across teams and external entities

Even better if:

• Understanding of games, betting, sports and igaming industry.

• Media contract management

• Interest in sports.

• Experience or coursework in contracts and regulatory law, litigation support or in-house legal routines (including internships).

• Availability to work on hybrid model and/or to relocate to São Paulo, Brazil, but fully remote applications will also be considered;

Location: &nbsp; This position may be performed remotely, but requires the flexibility and willingness to travel as needed.

The Opportunity

Help bring accurate, high-quality materials to the people who need them. As Specialist, MLR Submissions &amp; Production Quality Assurance, you will help move materials through Medical, Legal, and Regulatory (MLR) review and into print production and distribution. Your work will make submissions easier to review and help ensure final materials match the approved content.&nbsp;

You will prepare submissions in Veeva RAPID, organize supporting references, and link and tag claims to source documentation. Working with marketing, medical, review teams, and agency partners, you will perform quality assurance checks in Veeva PromoMats, resolve submission and production gaps, and keep work moving with clear priorities and timely communication.&nbsp;

Primary Responsibilities

• Prepare complete, accurate submission packages in Veeva RAPID so MLR reviewers have the materials and supporting documentation they need to begin review.&nbsp;

• Upload and organize supporting references, link and tag claims to the relevant source passages, and confirm that reference annotations are complete and easy for reviewers to follow.&nbsp;

• Check submission details, document naming, metadata, version history, and required supporting files to ensure materials meet established process requirements.&nbsp;

• Partner with content owners and agencies to resolve missing references, incomplete annotations, formatting issues, and other submission gaps before review; raise unresolved issues promptly.&nbsp;

• Support revisions and resubmissions, maintaining accurate claim-to-reference links and confirming that updates and supporting files belong to the correct document version.&nbsp;

• Perform quality assurance checks on final materials in Veeva PromoMats, comparing production files against MLR-approved content and confirming that required changes have been incorporated.&nbsp;

• Review copy, references, footnotes, required disclosures, layout, and production details. Identify discrepancies, coordinate corrections with internal teams and production partners, and confirm resolution before release.&nbsp;

• Complete assigned production approval and release steps for print production and distribution, consistent with established procedures and approval authority.&nbsp;

• Maintain clear submission and production status, communicate priorities and risks to deadlines early, and recommend practical improvements that reduce avoidable rework and turnaround time.&nbsp;

Qualifications and Key Success Factors

• Experience supporting biopharmaceutical promotional review, MLR submissions, editorial operations, or medical and marketing production, with examples of delivering accurate work against deadlines.&nbsp;

• Experience proofreading documents for print production, ensuring accuracy in spelling, grammar, punctuation, formatting, and consistency with final approved content before release to print vendors.&nbsp;

• Familiarity with preparing submission packages, managing references, and linking claims to supporting source documentation. Hands-on experience with Veeva PromoMats and Veeva MedProduction is required.&nbsp;

• Experience as an editor or medical editor, including proofreading, reference checking, and reviewing scientific or medical content, is required.&nbsp;

• Experience with medical production, promotional print production, or final material quality assurance, including comparing production proofs against approved content, is a plus.&nbsp;

• Strong attention to detail, demonstrated through identifying inconsistencies in copy, annotations, document versions, and production files and following corrections through to completion.&nbsp;

